<title>BRAZIL: Economist to replace Brazil Treasury chief.</title>
<headline>Economist to replace Brazil Treasury chief.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economist Augosto Guimaraes has been appointed to replace National Treasury head Murilo Portugal, Brazilian Finance Ministry officials said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Guimaraes, a London University-trained economist and former head of the Brazilian government's National Statistics Institute (IBGE), will take over on December 2, they said.</p>
<p>Portugal is leaving the Treasury to take up a position with the World Bank.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
</text>
